  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is rational. This corresponds to $M.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $2$ is less than $4$ and $2\\in Z.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}4}_{\u23df}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{2\\in Z}_{\u23df}}_{P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N\u2227P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\pi \\text{\u00a0is rational}}_{\u23df}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{2\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}4\\text{\u00a0and\u00a0}2\\in Z}_{\u23df}}_{N\\,\u2227\\,P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $M\u2227(N\u2227P).$",
